Section 50.
Officials of the City of Victorias.
– The present elective officials of the Municipality of Victorias shall continue to exercise their powers and functions until such time that a new election is held and the duly-elected officials shall have already qualified and assumed their offices. The appointive officials and employees of the Municipality of Victorias shall likewise continue exercising their functions and duties as such and they shall be automatically absorbed by the city government of the City of Victorias.
Section 51.
Succession Clause.
– The City of Victorias shall succeed to all the assets, properties, liabilities and obligations of the Municipality of Victorias.
Section 52.
Jurisdiction of the Province of Negros Occidental.
– The City of Victorias shall, unless otherwise provided by law, continue to be under the jurisdiction of the Province of Negros Occidental.
Section 53.
Term of Office.
– (a) The term of office of all local elective officials elected after the approval of this Act shall not exceed three (3) consecutive terms for a term of three (3) years each, or unless otherwise shortened or extended by Act of Congress.
(b) Voluntary renunciation of the office for any length of time shall not be considered as an interruption in the continuity of service for the full term for which the elective official concerned was elected.
Section 54.
Representative District.
– Until otherwise provided by law, the City of Victorias shall continue to be part of the Third Congressional District of the Province of Negros Occidental.
Section 55.
Separability Clause.
– If any part or provision of this Act is declared invalid or unconstitutional, the other parts or provisions thereof shall remain valid and effective.
Section 56.
Applicability of Laws.
– The provisions of Republic Act Numbered 7160, otherwise known as the Local Government Code of 1991, and other laws pertaining to the Province of Negros Occidental and such laws as are applicable to the component cities shall govern the City of Victorias insofar as they are not inconsistent with the provisions of this Act.
Section 57.
Repealing Clause.
– All laws, decrees, rules or regulations or parts thereof inconsistent with the provisions of this Act are hereby repealed, amended or modified accordingly.
Section 58.
Effectivity.
– This Act shall take effect upon its approval.
Approved, February 11, 1998.
