If the provincial governor approves the same, he shall affix his signature on each and every page thereof, otherwise, he shall veto it and return the same with his objections to the sanggunian which may proceed to reconsider the same. The sanggunian may override the veto of the provincial governor by two-thirds (2⁄3) vote of all its members, thereby making the ordinance or resolution effective for all legal intents and purposes.
