Section 28.
Implementing Rules and Regulations.
— Within sixty (60) days from the effectivity of this Act, the DTI Secretary shall, in consultation with other concerned government agencies, the industry representatives and nongovernment organizations, promulgate the necessary rules and regulations for the effective implementation of this Act.
Section 29.
Separability Clause.
— If any provision of this Act is held invalid or unconstitutional, the other provisions not affected thereby shall remain in full force and effect.
Section 30.
Repealing Clause.
— All laws, presidential decrees, executive orders, rules and regulations and other issuances or parts thereof which are inconsistent with the provisions of this Act are hereby repealed, amended or modified accordingly.
Section 31.
Effectivity.
— This Act shall take effect fifteen (15) days after its publication in the Official Gazette or in at least two (2) newspapers of general circulation in the Philippines.
